cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its results, please cite it as below."
title: "The four-speed lonely runner spectrum below 1/4: a kernel-checked formalization"
abstract: >-
  A complete formalization in Lean 4 with Mathlib of the statement that, for four distinct positive integer speeds,
  the values of the maximum loneliness ML below 1/4 are exactly j/(4j+2) with j >= 2 and j != 3 (the inclusion,
  the attainment of every value, and the equivalence), with no sorry, no native_decide and no axiom beyond
  propext, Classical.choice and Quot.sound. The proof uses a computer-generated certificate that the Lean kernel
  checks, an exact analysis of two infinite families on the critical tori, and one sporadic tuple. The theorem is
  not new: it is due to Yi, Gill and Bu (arXiv:2610.40694), with an effective computer-assisted proof, after
  Jain and Kravitz (Combinatorial Theory 6 (2026), Paper 1) and the conjecture of Fan and Sun
  (Electron. J. Combin. 33 (2026), P1.38); no first proof is claimed. The archive contains the paper, the 103 Lean
  modules of the dependency closure, the Rust certificate generators and a reproduction entry point (one module at
  a time, about 2.4 hours, 8.9 GB peak). The Lean modules, the Rust generators and the first draft of the paper
  were produced by an AI system (Claude, Anthropic); the questions, directions and the decision to formalize this
  statement came from Vico Bonfioli. The paper has not been peer reviewed. No proof of the lonely runner
  conjecture is claimed.
authors:
  - family-names: Bonfioli
    given-names: Vico
